<title>JAPAN: Batteries sold in Japan in Nov contain less lead.</title>
<headline>Batteries sold in Japan in Nov contain less lead.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lead content of batteries sold in Japan in November fell 2.2 percent from the same month last year to 26,097 tonnes, the Japan Storage Battery Association said on Friday.</p>
<p>Lead content of batteries sold in October (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Nov 96	 yr/yr change</p>
<p> Total	     26,097	  -2.2 pct</p>
<p>   Automotive    20,853	  -3.0 pct</p>
<p>   Industrial     3,754	 +12.1 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: Automotive includes a small quantity of lead used in two-wheeled vehicles. Industrial use includes stationary power sources and electric vehicles such as forklifts.)</p>
<p>Automotive battery shipments in November (1,000 units):</p>
<p>			Nov 96	yr/yr change</p>
<p> TOTAL		2,441	  -3.6 pct</p>
<p> Domestic	   2,407	  -2.8 pct</p>
<p>   New cars	 1,017	 +10.2 pct</p>
<p>   Replacement    1,390	 -10.5 pct</p>
<p> Exports		 34	 -41.2 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: Battery shipment totals exclude two-wheeled vehicles.)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
